# Keep the build context small, but never hide a source file from the builder.
#
# This previously excluded `frontend` wholesale. backend/Dockerfile does not need it,
# but Railway's auto-detected builder does - it reads the root package.json, sees a
# workspace and copies frontend/package.json. Excluding the directory made that file
# "not found" and failed the build before anything else could go wrong.
#
# So exclude only what is genuinely disposable: installed packages, build output,
# secrets, uploads and logs.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Uploaded files - large, and restored from a volume rather than baked into an image.
backend/storage/apk/*
backend/storage/files/*
backend/storage/tmp/*
!backend/storage/**/.gitkeep

**/*.log
.git
.github
